		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Numerical Analysis/Physics Software Engineer Wanted]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=27615#p27615"><![CDATA[
Pilots learn to fly planes using flight simulators.  Doctors learn to do medical procedures using the simulators we create. Medical Simulation Corporation (MSC) develops high-tech simulation training programs used by doctors, nurses and other medical professionals. We have been doing this for more than 12 years and are the worldwide leader in simulation training.<br><br>MSC is based in Denver, Colorado with 300 days of sunshine each year - more than San Diego or Miami Beach (see <a href="http://www.metrodenver.org" class="postlink">http://www.metrodenver.org</a> for more info). We offer a competitive salary and a comprehensive benefit package including 401k, medical, dental, vision, life insurance, FSA and a range of optional benefits. Dress is casual. We do offer relocation assistance.<br><br><strong class="text-strong"><span style="text-decoration:underline">About the Position</span></strong><br><br>As an Analysis/Games/Physics/Graphic Engineer, you will be challenged to develop Global Finite Element Models (GFEM) for modeling and interaction.  You will have a broad variety of tasks within the global FE and deformable modeling and simulation solutions.  Working in Denver in a strong team of game physics and numerical analysts, your principle activities will include:<br><br>• Develop numerical methods for large rotation FE model<br>• Deformable modeling formulation that stands up to clinical interrogation and interaction<br>• Electrophysiology<br>• Fluid dynamics<br>• Collision detection of deformable models<br>• Ensure methods development for all modeling and simulation<br>• Full scale validation of FE and deformable modeling<br>• Methods and tools development to support program requirements<br>• Graphics shader support for the deformable modeling results <br> <br>As the successful candidate you will be able to demonstrate the following skills and competencies:<br>• Previous finite element analysis experience, MATLAB experience<br>• Implementation and optimization of numerical methods<br>• Strong C++ and OO skills<br>• Demonstrated growth in technical responsibility during your career<br>• A background in game physics, stress or numerical analysis is desirable<br>• Strong team player - as the interactions with customers will call upon good interpersonal skills<br><br>Apply if you think quickly on your feet and have the ability to apply new techniques in creative ways. We’re looking forward to having you join our team.<br><br>Please submit your resume to:<br><a href="http://tbe.taleo.net/NA4/ats/careers/requisition.jsp?org=MEDSIMULATION&amp;cws=1&amp;rid=80" class="postlink">http://tbe.taleo.net/NA4/ats/careers/re ... s=1&amp;rid=80</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=9240">MedSimulation</a> — Mon Apr 09, 2012 8:51 pm</p><hr />
